{
  "requirement": "The `PlainText` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct PlainText;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for PlainText;\nimpl Debug for PlainText;\nimpl Default for PlainText;\nimpl OutlineLang for PlainText;\nimpl Copy for PlainText;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.PlainText`**\n1. `PlainText` is a public unit struct.\n2. It has the trait implementations Clone, Debug, Default, OutlineLang and Copy.\n3. Its `OutlineLang` implementation supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Struct and trait implementations:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` generates rustdoc for the SDK. It compares each declaration against the book. Through `check_declaration`, it asserts that the set of documented trait impls equals the set rustdoc reports (`Trait implementations for {id}`). A missing or extra Clone, Debug, Default, Copy or OutlineLang impl on `PlainText` would fail it. The same test also compiles the Habeas consumer against the SDK.\n- **Extension rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` asserts `PlainText.name() == \"plain-text\"` and that `extensions()` is empty. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors]` loads `missing.unclaimed`, `README` and `missing`, none of which any language claims. Each is outlined as plain text.\n- **Selection rule:** `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` covers the plain-text items.\n  - A root item spans the whole text, and an empty file yields only the root.\n  - Blank lines are skipped.\n  - Line items have kind `line` and a selector of the form `line@` followed by 12 hex digits, equal to the first 12 characters of the structural hash.\n  - Duplicate lines share a selector, and distinct lines get different selectors.\n  - `select` returns the line text.\n  - Reflowed text keeps the same selectors, structural hash and fingerprint.\n  - Reordered or joined lines change the structural hash.\n- **Fingerprint rule:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[plain_line_fingerprints_use_sha256_words_without_losing_boundaries]` asserts a known SHA-256 value, whitespace normalisation, word-boundary preservation, and the scheme `plain-text-structural-v1:own-v1`. The fingerprint equality and inequality assertions in `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` add further coverage.\n- **Structural search:** `outline_only_languages_report_unsupported_structural_search` shows `PlainText` rejects structural search with a plain-text message. The subject's text does not require this.\n\n**Delegation and marking**\nThe detailed items and fingerprints rules belong to the refining requirements `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.items` and `requirements.sdk.sources.plain-text.fingerprints`. These tests also carry those references. All relevant tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. I found no unmarked relevant test and no assertion gap.",
